izens and their families  through a number of programs that we  offer for free to a senior citizen and  that's everything from pantry to  transportation to respite care and even  home repair oh my goodness and um i've  volunteered and i've done some of those  grocery deliveries especially during the  pandemic yes some of these people are in  a bad way and they they need help how  was life during the pandemic for  non-profits like yours for ours really  we had to make a pivot in regards to how  we performed our services and how we  gave because it brought  a huge light upon the real need in the  valley and so our seniors  came out in full force in regards to the  need because  organizations like yourselves like news  8 brought some awareness to what we do  and and how we do it and so  we became really creative because of the  pandemic there were several different  rules and how we approached our seniors  and so we put safety measures in place  in order for us to continue to feed them  to provide assistance in housing  respite care and like i said  transportation  but really it more than doubled our  clientele because of the pandemic and so  we heavily rely upon our community  partners to come together to bring a  collaborative effort to make that larger  impact and this is a big fundraiser for  you if people are interested and would  still like to come and get tickets where  do they go please visit our website  hhov.org  you'll find it on our day at the derby  and our tickets right now are going for  a hundred dollars we hope to see  everyone yeah lots of food fun drinks  and good entertainment and yes helping  seniors in our valley who need it so  much the need is still there right it  exists and we've been doing this for the  last 22 years well great organization  great to see you nina thank you  fantastic in your hatred we should see  you on saturday
 

